# Required: your OpenRouter API key (https://openrouter.ai/keys)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# Output format (reel | youtube) and target length for youtube runs.
# reel    = vertical 9:16 short (~30-60s) — the default
# youtube = landscape 16:9 long-form: chaptered script, per-chapter TTS + rendering, 1280x720
#           thumbnail, youtube.md metadata (title/description/tags/chapter timestamps).
#           The video-model default becomes alibaba/wan-2.6 (cheaper, 15s clips); switch back
#           per run with --video-model google/veo-3.1-lite if you prefer the Veo look.
# REELMAESTRO_FORMAT=reel
# REELMAESTRO_MINUTES=3        # youtube target length in minutes (1-12)

# Quality/cost tier presetting the model defaults below (draft | standard | premium).
# draft   = cheapest models (Haiku script, Nano Banana 2 images), validation off — rough previews
# standard = the regular defaults (this is what you get when unset)
# premium = Opus script, Veo 3.1 Fast at 1080p, deepest validation — final renders
# Any explicit model override below (or its CLI flag) still wins over the tier's pick.
# REELMAESTRO_QUALITY=standard

# Optional model overrides (CLI flags take precedence over these; unset values come from the tier).
# REELMAESTRO_TEXT_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
# REELMAESTRO_JUDGE_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash   # multimodal scene-consistency judge
# REELMAESTRO_IMAGE_MODEL=google/gemini-3-pro-image
# REELMAESTRO_TTS_MODEL=google/gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview
# REELMAESTRO_MUSIC_MODEL=google/lyria-3-pro-preview
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_MODEL=google/veo-3.1-lite
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_RESOLUTION=720p                 # accepted: 720p or 1080p (case-insensitive)
# Video generation can instead use the private local MiniMax H3 REST service. Other stages remain
# on OpenRouter. Local H3 uses exact 544x960 (reel) / 960x544 (youtube), costs $0 metered, and
# never falls back or re-rolls through a hosted video provider.
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_PROVIDER=local                   # default: openrouter
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8088
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_API_TOKEN=replace-with-h3-token  # H3_STUDIO_KEY is also accepted as fallback
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_INPUT_MODE=first-frame           # first-frame | text
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_SEED=42
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_STEPS=50                         # validated against service discovery
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_WAIT_TIMEOUT=60                  # minutes; accepted jobs remain resumable
# REELMAESTRO_VIDEO_SIZE=544x960                     # exact local H3 dimensions; YouTube default 960x544
# REELMAESTRO_MAX_COST=5.00                          # abort before paid calls above this estimated USD total
#
# Video model options (per-second cost at 720p, July 2026 OpenRouter pricing; all support
# image-to-video with a first frame, which is how scenes are animated):
#   Model                        $/s      Clip lengths   Notes
#   alibaba/wan-2.6              ~0.04    2-15s          cheapest; 16:9+9:16; youtube default
#   google/veo-3.1-lite          0.05     4/6/8s only    reel default, proven in this pipeline
#   bytedance/seedance-2.0-fast  ~0.054   2-15s          fast tier; first+last frame control
#   bytedance/seedance-2.0       ~0.067   2-15s          strong character consistency
#   google/veo-3.1-fast          0.10     4/6/8s only    premium-tier pick (0.12 at 1080p)
#   kwaivgi/kling-v3.0-std       ~0.126   3-15s          mid-tier alternative
# Models with flexible clip lengths fit long scene windows without slow-motion stretching.
# Unknown video models are estimated conservatively at $0.40/s and marked as an estimate guess.
# REELMAESTRO_VALIDATE_SCENE=2                      # off | 2 | 3 candidates judged per scene
# REELMAESTRO_VOICE=Kore

# Image model options (set REELMAESTRO_IMAGE_MODEL above or --image-model; swaps EVERY image gen:
# character references, scene stills, and the poster). The model MUST accept image input, since the
# pipeline conditions each scene on reference images — all the options below do.
# Discover current ones: curl -s "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models" | grep -i image
#
# "x" is the rough per-reel cost relative to the default (gemini-3-pro-image).
#   Model                              vs default   Notes
#   google/gemini-3-pro-image          1x (default) best coherence + cross-scene consistency
#   google/gemini-3.1-flash-image      ~0.5x        Nano Banana 2 — half the cost, faster, weaker coherence
#   google/gemini-2.5-flash-image      ~0.3x        Older flash — a downgrade, skip
#   openai/gpt-5-image-mini            ~1.2x        OpenAI; strong instruction-following
#   openai/gpt-5.4-image-2             ~4x          Newest OpenAI; best prompt adherence + structure
#   openai/gpt-5-image                 ~5x          OpenAI flagship image, max quality
# Going up a tier also lowers --validate-scene re-rolls (fewer defects to re-roll), so the effective
# cost gap is smaller than it looks. To save money, set the flash model above. OpenAI models are a
# different family — smoke-test one scene first, since the multi-reference payload may behave
# differently than the Gemini path.

# Voice: if REELMAESTRO_VOICE/--voice is unset, it's auto-picked from the script's narrator
# gender (male -> Puck, female/neutral -> Kore). Set it here to force one voice for every run.
# Voice depends on REELMAESTRO_TTS_MODEL — each model has its own set (use --voice for one-offs).
# Discover current voices: curl -s "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models?output_modalities=speech"
#
# google/gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview (default) — 30 voices. Hints: Kore=warm/curious (default),
# Charon=deep/serious, Puck=bright/conversational, Aoede=friendly, Schedar=neutral, Fenrir=energetic:
#   Zephyr Puck Charon Kore Fenrir Leda Orus Aoede Callirrhoe Autonoe
#   Enceladus Iapetus Umbriel Algieba Despina Erinome Algenib Rasalgethi Laomedeia Achernar
#   Alnilam Schedar Gacrux Pulcherrima Achird Zubenelgenubi Vindemiatrix Sadachbia Sadaltager Sulafat
#
# x-ai/grok-voice-tts-1.0: eve ara rex sal leo
#
# mistralai/voxtral-mini-tts-2603 (emotion-tagged): en_paul_{neutral,happy,sad,excited,confident,
#   cheerful,frustrated,angry}, gb_oliver_{neutral,excited,curious,confident,...}, gb_jane_{neutral,
#   sad,curious,sarcasm,...}, fr_marie_{neutral,happy,excited,curious,sad,angry}
#
# microsoft/mai-voice-2 (multilingual): en-US-Harper:MAI-Voice-2 es-MX-Valeria:MAI-Voice-2
#   fr-FR-Soleil:MAI-Voice-2 de-DE-Klaus:MAI-Voice-2

# Local word-level caption timing (whisper-timestamped). Not an OpenRouter call.
# REELMAESTRO_WHISPER_CMD=whisper_timestamped
# REELMAESTRO_WHISPER_MODEL=base
# Caption appearance (burst | karaoke | boxed | minimal) and installed font family.
# REELMAESTRO_CAPTION_STYLE=burst
# REELMAESTRO_CAPTION_FONT=DejaVu Sans

# Output toggles (also available as CLI flags --no-captions / --no-narration / --scene-seconds).
# REELMAESTRO_NO_CAPTIONS=1    # don't burn captions into the video
# REELMAESTRO_NO_NARRATION=1   # no spoken voiceover (silent or music-only video)
# REELMAESTRO_SCENE_SECONDS=4  # per-scene length used when narration is disabled

# Optional local Studio server (Node.js 22.13+). Export these into its process environment;
# Studio does not automatically load this file. See studio/README.md.
# Connect the provider in Studio Settings or export OPENROUTER_API_KEY when starting the server.
# REELMAESTRO_PORT=3000
# REELMAESTRO_HOST=127.0.0.1  # Set a specific LAN IPv4 address only on a trusted network; no login/TLS.
# Use absolute paths for overrides. Defaults are relative to the repository, not the browser.
# REELMAESTRO_OUT_DIR=/absolute/path/to/reel-maestro/out
# REELMAESTRO_STATE_DIR=/absolute/path/to/reel-maestro/.studio-state
# REELMAESTRO_BINARY=/absolute/path/to/reel-maestro/target/debug/reelmaestro
